tive files / 14 cases pass, plus the two guard Node cases and direct value/byte/decoder/refusal/response boundary assertions. Retained my initial incorrect nonexistent --project node startup failure (no cases) and native sandbox loopback EPERM (before cases); corrected project selection and permitted local-loopback run pass. These are local/TEST witnesses, with no browser, provider, publication or deployment acceptance claim.\n\nFrozen checker evidence: /private/tmp/checker-k1-review-q5x77m7b/checker-evidence-manifest.json, 2732 bytes, SHA-256 d46574e00b786f6b4ac7b21a1f1d6dc0cf164c3c0731f2d085f3fccebd0bd878. Builder/planner may read/stable-copy only that manifest and its twelve individually hash-bound regular leaves; all freeze forever, never execute or edit originals, no adjacent directory/source/dependency/tool grant. Approval is exact-head review; landing and full artifact succession remain separate.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:529664807658c3bc1fb28d865dc9de0e08191cd1","binding":"assigned","head":"5706ac22a6a9e34bb4f8d9fa57589e7cb9ec383e","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a5917640636330a6984273af64ea722df146af67\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1b758ab79406a126c390fca8a5e14b0b76fa9405\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ab6a92c3274fc0a18fd906edc9f797f2977204a7","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}